/*
  lemmas.spthy -- the shared [reuse] lemma spine (repo MEMORY.md lesson 15): the boundary facts proven
  ONCE per profile so every profile's secrecy pair terminates over the layered state space. Included by
  base.spthy BEFORE any profile's own lemmas.

  H_leak_routes is the T6 (S) BOUNDARY LIST: the single enumerated set of human mistakes through which a
  Secret can reach the adversary. It is the union over BOTH variants -- the legacy sender/receiver and the
  full-interface screens -- so it holds for either. A disjunct whose action fact the compiled variant
  never emits is simply unsatisfiable, which costs nothing.

    legacy      : credulous fingerprint compare (Mistake) | PW misdeliver (MisdeliveredPw)
                  | PW in-band (LeakPw)
    screens A   : badkey compare (Mistake) | subject transcribe leak (SubjectLeak)
                  | out-of-order send (SendPremature) | To-field slip (MisaddressedSend)
    screens B/C : Forward to a keyless third party (ForwardedOutside)
                  | pw entered at the phishing page (PwEnteredAtImpostor)

  NOT a leak route: PlaintextAtProvider (the TLS misroute) emits NO Out, so it never yields K(m) -- it is
  a NAMED unsafe outcome an RFC lemma forbids, which is what keeps breach <-> mistake honest.
*/

// (S) BOUNDARY LIST -- every way the MESSAGE crosses the boundary. Profiles' secrecy lemmas consume this.
lemma H_leak_routes [reuse]:
  all-traces
  "All m #s #k.
     Secret(m)@s & K(m)@k
   ==> (Ex p vid #d. Mistake(p, vid)@d)
     | (Ex p #d. LeakPw(p)@d)
     | (Ex p #d. MisdeliveredPw(p)@d)
     | (Ex p #d. SubjectLeak(p)@d)
     | (Ex p #d. SendPremature(p)@d)
     | (Ex p #d. ForwardedOutside(p)@d)
     | (Ex p #d. MisaddressedSend(p)@d)"

// the passphrase reaches the adversary only through a degraded share outcome, or by being entered at the
// impostor (phishing) page on Blake's Screen B.
lemma H_pw_stays_oob [reuse]:
  all-traces
  "All pw #c #k.
     PwCreated(pw)@c & K(pw)@k
   ==> (Ex p #d. LeakPw(p)@d)
     | (Ex p #d. MisdeliveredPw(p)@d)
     | (Ex p #d. PwEnteredAtImpostor(p)@d)"

// a generated private key never reaches the adversary (it never leaves !OwnSk).
lemma H_sk_secret [reuse, heuristic=C]:
  all-traces
  "All p sk #g #k. OwnSkGen(p, sk)@g & K(sk)@k ==> F"

// STRUCTURAL: a message is encrypted to the correspondent ('Blake') only, unless the fingerprint compare
// was answered credulously (a Mistake) and it went to a non-correspondent. K-free, so it is cheap and
// prunes the K(m) search for every profile that consumes it.
lemma H_encto_shape [reuse]:
  all-traces
  "All m rcpt #e.
     EncTo(m, rcpt)@e
   ==> (rcpt = 'Blake')
     | (Ex p vid #d. Mistake(p, vid)@d)"
